---
import { journey } from "../../data/journey";
import { stateOptions } from "../../lib/states";

const ask = journey.flatMap((stage) => stage.modules).find((m) => m.slug === "01-collection")!.ask;
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, "/");
const film = (name: string) => `${base}film/${name}`;
const filmScript = [
  "Module 1 comes down to one idea.",
  "No errors describes the program. Only a coverage record, written against what should exist, describes the data. And anything it can't see, it calls unknown. Never zero.",
  "Tuesday. Kick adds a tidy rule. An \"St.\" in a name means State. The table now lists State Lambert.",
  "St. Lambert (voicemail): Hi, this is St. Lambert soccer. Saint, as in the saint. Your table says State Lambert. We are not a state school. Please fix it.",
  "Kick: Fixed. Saint stays Saint. One line.",
  "The code is fixed in a minute. Friday's table isn't. Ask the eight sites again and you get Tuesday's pages, not Friday's. Dunmore's might not answer at all.",
  "So Riley asks Kick one more thing.",
  "Riley: Can you rebuild Friday's table from the pages you kept, without asking a single site again, and show me you did?",
];
const heads = [
  ["total", "100 visits across the network"],
  ["floor", "At least 100 visits, from eight of ten clinics. Two have not reported."],
  ["zeros", "100 visits. Two clinics reported none."],
  ["unknown", "Visits unknown"],
];
const next = [
  ["../01-collection-field-work/?from=carry-it#assistant", "Test your own assistant", "on the pages Kick got, with a gap nothing mentions"],
  ["../01-collection-field-work/?from=carry-it#statistics", "Statistics of the gap", "missingness mechanisms, and bounds that depend on each other"],
  ["../01-collection-field-work/?from=carry-it#platform", "How Touchline builds it", "merge, atomic write and reruns"],
  ["../01-collection-field-work/?from=carry-it#lab", "The lab", "write Friday's coverage record in Python"],
];
---

<section id="carry-it">
  <h2>Carry it: the same number, twice</h2>
  <p>A health network has ten clinics that report patient visits each week. For week 9 you hold the same spreadsheet in two worlds: eight rows, sum 100.</p>
  <div class="cv-twins">
    <div>
      <h3>World A</h3>
      <p>The other two clinics each sent a file with a header and no rows. Both were closed that week for refitting, and the closure notices are on file.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>World B</h3>
      <p>The other two sent nothing. Nobody has heard from them.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="cv-twins">
    <div>
      <h3>World C</h3>
      <p>The other two each sent a file with a header and no rows. Nothing in either file says which week it covers, and there is no closure notice.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="cv-check" data-once="transfer">
    {(["a", "b"] as const).map((w) => (
      <div class="cv-line" data-q data-type="select" data-answer={w === "a" ? "total" : "floor"}
        data-why={w === "a" ? "100 visits across the network. The two closed clinics answered, proved their week, and saw nobody: empty, so zero is true." : "At least 100, from eight of ten. The two silent clinics are unavailable: unknown, not zero."}
        data-wrong={JSON.stringify(w === "a" ? { floor: "World A's two clinics did answer, with proof. Nothing is unknown.", zeros: "True, and it is the same total. Choose the headline that states it plainly.", unknown: "Every clinic is accounted for. The total is known." } : { total: "Two clinics never answered. 100 is only what you hold.", zeros: "Nobody reported zero. Silence is unknown, not zero.", unknown: "You do know at least 100. Say that." })}>
        <label><span>World {w.toUpperCase()}: which headline is honest?</span>
          <select data-save={`transfer-${w}`}><option value="">Choose</option>{heads.map(([k, t]) => <option value={k}>{t}</option>)}</select>
        </label>
        <p class="cv-fb" role="status"></p>
      </div>
    ))}
    <div class="cv-line" data-q data-type="select" data-answer="unavailable" data-why="Unavailable. A file arrived and cannot prove it is week 9's. The same rule as a schedule page that cannot prove its season." data-wrong={JSON.stringify({ empty: "Empty needs proof of which week the file covers. These files cannot give it.", "no-collector": "The files open fine. They just cannot prove their week." })}>
      <label><span>World C: what state are those two clinics in for week 9?</span>
        <select data-save="transfer-c"><option value="">Choose a state</option>{stateOptions.map(([k, n]) => <option value={k}>{n}</option>)}</select>
      </label>
      <p class="cv-fb" role="status"></p>
    </div>
    <div data-q data-type="range" data-answer="400,520" data-why="400 to 520. The floor is what you hold. The ceiling adds the most the silent clinic could have seen: 5 days at 24. A known limit on the missing unit turns a lower bound into a range, as the points rule did for Dunmore.">
      <p class="cv-qlabel">A week later you hold 400 visits from nine clinics. The tenth is still silent. Its licence allows at most 24 visits a day, and it opens five days a week. What are the lowest and highest totals the network could have?</p>
      <div class="cv-row cv-fillin"><span>Between</span><input inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Lowest total" data-save="clinic-low" /><span>and</span><input inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Highest total" data-save="clinic-high" /></div>
      <p class="cv-fb" role="status"></p>
    </div>
    <p class="cv-once">One attempt at all four.</p>
    <button type="button" data-submit>Check my four</button>
    <p class="cv-fb" role="status" data-need></p>
    <div class="cv-reveal"><p>World C holds the same files as World A and supports only World B's headline, because its files cannot prove their week. Same number, three worlds, and only the record tells them apart.</p></div>
  </div>

  <h3>The one ask</h3>
  <p>Take this to any AI that collects anything for you.</p>
  <div class="cv-prompt">
    <p data-copy-text>{ask}</p>
    <button type="button" data-copy data-label="Copy the ask">Copy the ask</button>
  </div>

  <h3>Then Tuesday</h3>
  <p>A minute to close the module: the idea in one breath, and the bug that opens the next one.</p>
  <figure class="cv-film">
    <video controls playsinline preload="metadata" poster={film("monday-then-tuesday.jpg")} aria-label="Monday, Then Tuesday, a one-minute closing film for Module 1">
      <source src={film("monday-then-tuesday.mp4")} type="video/mp4" />
      <track kind="captions" src={film("monday-then-tuesday.vtt")} srclang="en" label="English" default />
    </video>
    <figcaption>Monday, Then Tuesday. Every count on screen is the sample's.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <details class="cv-more">
    <summary>Read the film's narration</summary>
    {filmScript.map((x) => <p>{x}</p>)}
  </details>
  <p class="cv-next">Riley's question is where Module 2 starts. <a href="../02-archive/">Module 2: The raw archive</a></p>

  <h3>Go further first</h3>
  <p>Each of these is optional and stands alone, on the <a href="../01-collection-field-work/?from=carry-it">field work page</a>.</p>
  <ul class="cv-next-links">
    {next.map(([href, name, what]) => <li><a href={href}>{name}</a><span>{what}</span></li>)}
  </ul>
  <button type="button" class="cv-quiet" data-reset>Clear my answers and start this module again</button>
</section>
